### Parser-cache diagnosis and tested proposal

Cargo's diagnostic log identified generated `parser.c` as newer than its build-script output checkpoint. Restoring that first-build cache repeatedly reruns Anicca and dependent core checks. The cause is generated-output timestamp ordering, not a changed project source file. Temporary diagnostic branch removed after its completed run/log capture; the normal validation branch remains for its scoped cache.

| Experiment | Result and decision |
| --- | --- |
| Actual Anicca first-build cache restored three times | All three checks rebuild Anicca; false invalidation reproduced locally on Linux. |
| Stamp only freshly written parser C/header/native archives with a stable timestamp | All three restored checks stay fresh. Parser C, header and native archive SHA-256 values are byte-identical to baseline. Local correctness gate passes; whole-workflow timing of this proposal remains untested. |
| Missing parser C, header and archive | Each regenerates correctly; the next unchanged check stays fresh. Recovery is retained. |
| Real grammar token mutation and restoration | Changing `for` to `foreach` changes accepted syntax; restoring the source restores the original syntax. Real input changes still invalidate. |
| Native compiler wrapper mutation and restoration | Tool change is detected and recompiles; the next check stays fresh. Original compiler selection restored. |
| Cache generation includes build helpers | Proposed key refreshes for build-script/helper changes while ordinary application edits retain the dependency bucket. All 19 local cache tests pass in 12.828s. This extension is part of the saved proposal, not the current main default. |
| Actual copied Interface icon-generator probe | All three first-cache restores already stay fresh. No icon-generator change is justified. |

Decision: preserve the parser/cache-key proposal for review; do not claim a qualified whole-job gain or promote it without that measurement. Candidate: `target/build-iteration/actions-consolidation/parser-cache-candidate.patch`; isolated checkout: `target/build-iteration/actions-consolidation/parser-worktree/`. Grammar and compiler probes were restored, and the temporary example was moved to the receipts directory. Main production files are unchanged by this proposal.

### Optimized native linker comparison

Full local Lince preparation completed with `--release --features instinct,park --target x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu`, warnings denied, portable Rust CPU settings and incrementality off. It retained maximum optimization and unwind recovery. The private-daemon restart took 49m30s after the interrupted shared-daemon preparation; these setup durations are not linker timings. The saved binary reports UI/Instinct/Park enabled and revision `unknown`; this is a local optimized comparison artifact, not a published release.

Compared Ubuntu24.04 mold 2.30.0 (matching the Actions version) with verified official Wild 0.9.0 on identical saved objects/libraries, after one warm-up per linker. Balanced order: A1/B1/B2/A2/A3/B3. Input SHA-256 values remained unchanged.

| Check | mold 2.30 | Wild 0.9 | Result |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Final optimized link, three samples | Median 2.327s; range 2.322–2.336s | Median 1.389s; range 1.288–1.483s | 0.938s saved, 40.30% of the final link stage. Link gate passes; this is not a whole-build percentage. |
| Read-only arithmetic CLI workload | Median of group medians 104.60ms | 98.93ms | Correct output; no measured slowdown. |
| Read-only branching CLI workload | 64.52ms | 60.78ms | Correct output; no measured slowdown. |
| Packaging with the normal Linux script | 320.46 MB archive | 314.76 MB archive | Both pass checksums, metadata, licenses and exact packaged-binary checks. Packaging timings were validation only. |

Runtime order matches the linker order, with three groups of 20 invocations per workload per linker. Build-info/help outputs and shared-library requirements match. Both retain x86-64 PIE, RELRO/BIND_NOW, non-executable stack and unwind sections. No GUI/frame-time performance claim is made. Initial replay preflight encountered a response-file argument list; the harness was corrected before timed linking, with the original captured inputs unchanged.

Decision: the linker component passes its local link/runtime/package gates. Keep Actions on mold while actual hosted job gains remain unqualified; local development remains on Wild. No Actions default or release optimization/CPU/hardening flag was changed. Task 3.1 subsequently completed its Actions qualification; see the hosted result below. The separate Nix source-package dry-run uses Rust 1.95 rather than repository/Actions 1.96 and lists 1,793 derivations; no source-package linker comparison was started, so task 3.2 remains open.

Receipts for all current experiments: `target/build-iteration/actions-consolidation/`. Existing Actionlint/ShellCheck and workflow condition checks passed; the applicable-rule search found no pipe-prefixed build requirement in Lince.lingua. No pre-existing product defect was repaired. The fixed task IDs/count in Build.md were preserved.

